  "answer": "Mr. Darbey is an officer of the Hussars, and his military status is directly connected to his being seen by The Dean and spoken to by Sheba. In the evidence, Darbey and Major Tarver are described as having 'ridden over from Durnstone' to visit the Dean, and Darbey is referred to as 'Mr. Darbey' while Tarver is 'Major Tarver'. The Dean initially mistakes Darbey's name as 'Mr. Garvey', but Sheba corrects him, saying 'Mr. Darbey!'. This interaction occurs because Darbey, as an officer, has come to the Deanery, and Sheba speaks to him during the visit. The graph context shows that The Dean 'OPPOSES' Nugent Darbey, and Sheba is the Dean's daughter, linking the characters. Thus, Darbey's status as an officer of the Hussars is the reason for his presence at the Deanery, where he is seen by The Dean and spoken to by Sheba.",
